# Build one Elf who walks through every shape of the multiclass experience
# penalty, and photograph his character sheet four times on the way.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. bd inc-by8. Character::XPPenalty (src/Create.cpp) used to
# ask whether the character's HIGHEST class was one his race favours and charge
# a flat 25% when it was not. The rule Brian ruled on removes every favoured
# class and every prestige class from the comparison, then charges 20% for each
# class that is left standing two or more levels below the highest class that
# is left. The costs add.
#
# THE ORACLE is the sheet's Basics block. src/Sheet.cpp:62-67 prints a
# " Penal <n>%" line when the penalty is positive and prints nothing at all
# when it is zero, so the absence of the line is as readable as its presence.
#
# WHY AN ELF, AND WHY THESE THREE CLASSES. A standard Elf favours Mage and
# Ranger (lib/races.irh:967). Barbarian, Rogue and Warrior are therefore all
# counted, none of them is a prestige class, and none of them has an attribute
# gate or an alignment that fights the other two. One character can then hold
# every shape the rule has:
#
#   xpa  Barbarian 3                 THE CONTROL. One counted class, so there
#                                    is nothing to compare it against and no
#                                    penalty. He must read the same on a build
#                                    with the defect and a build without it.
#   xpb  Barbarian 3 / Rogue 1       20%. The rogue stands two below the
#                                    barbarian.
#   xpc  + Warrior 1                 40%. Two classes stand two below the
#                                    barbarian, and the costs add. This is the
#                                    case that proves the stacking, and the
#                                    only one the old flat figure could never
#                                    produce.
#   xpd  Barbarian 3 / Rogue 2 /     Nothing. Every counted class is now
#        Warrior 2                   within one level of the highest.
#
# Measured on builds differing only in src/Create.cpp:
#                                        before      after
#   Barbarian 3                          none        none
#   Barbarian 3 / Rogue 1                25%         20%
#   Barbarian 3 / Rogue 1 / Warrior 1    25%         40%
#   Barbarian 3 / Rogue 2 / Warrior 2    25%         none
#
# tools/check_xp_penalty_rule.sh reads these four dumps. It also reads the two
# characters this script does not build: the prestige case
# (tools/keys/prestige-assassin.keys) and the within-one-level case
# (tools/keys/xp-penalty-crash.keys).
#
# THE TWO IDIOMS THAT LOOK ODD, and both are the game, not the script.
#
# 1. After a level is gained the character sheet is stale, and whether a dialog
#    is still open depends on whether that level asked for a feat. So every
#    level ends with one ESC -- which closes the dialog if there is one, and
#    otherwise leaves the sheet for the map -- followed by
#    @until "Gender" d, which opens the sheet again only if it is not already
#    there. Pressing ESC blindly until the map appears is NOT safe: ESC on the
#    map opens the System Menu, which this script has no key to leave.
# 2. A level can ask three different questions and each class words its feat
#    menu differently ("Advancing as a Warrior, choose a Warrior Feat:"), so
#    the whole group of @while lines is written out twice. A menu that opens
#    after the group has been passed would otherwise swallow every later key.
#
# SEED. The attribute rolls and the offered feats vary with the seed, so the
# feat picks stay positional and a seed is passed.

a
n
y
@choose "Elf"
@choose "Elf (Standard)"
@choose "Barbarian"
a
@choose "Neutral"
@until "Unspent Skill Ranks" a
@cursorto:mark "Athletics" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Climb" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Craft" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Healing" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Intimidate" DOWN
RIGHT*3
ENTER y
a
@until "Afoot" ESC
s
w
@expect "Enter wizard mode"
y
w
DOWN DOWN
SPACE
ESC

@until "Gender" d
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
ESC
@until "Gender" d
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
ESC
@until "Gender" d
@expect "Class  Barbarian 3"
@dump:xpa

M
@choose "Rogue"
ESC
@until "Gender" d
@expect "Rogue 0"
G
@choose "Rogue"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
ESC
@until "Gender" d
@expect "Class  Barbarian 3"
@expect "Rogue 1"
@dump:xpb

M
@choose "Warrior"
ESC
@until "Gender" d
@expect "Warrior 0"
G
@choose "Warrior"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
ESC
@until "Gender" d
@expect "Class  Barbarian 3"
@expect "Warrior 1"
@dump:xpc

G
@choose "Rogue"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
ESC
@until "Gender" d
@expect "Rogue 2"
G
@choose "Warrior"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Barbarian Feat" a
@while "Rogue Feat" a
@while "Warrior Feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
ESC
@until "Gender" d
@expect "Class  Barbarian 3"
@expect "Warrior 2"
@dump:xpd
ESC
@quit
